      "description": "June 2026 CPI Falls to 3.5%, Core CPI to 2.6%",
      "details": "The U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics released the Consumer Price Index (CPI) for June 2026, showing the annual inflation rate fell to 3.5% from 4.2% in May, the first decline in five months. The core CPI, excluding volatile food and energy, also decreased to 2.6% from 2.9%. This data indicates a cooling of inflation, which can be a positive signal for consumer purchasing power. This could lead to a boost in consumer confidence and discretionary spending, potentially improving ROAS and lowering CPA for a DTC food gifting brand.",
